    {
      "ply": 25,
      "san": "Qd3",
      "human_san": "Qd3",
      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "Of course Lilienthal declines the Queen\nexchange and prefers to use his Queen to help pushing the central pawns.",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "The most accurate move, maintaining White's advantage (+0.30, Stockfish:16), as [pv:Qd3 Nbd7 Ne2 O-O O-O] keeps White's pieces actively placed and improves their overall activity\u2014active pieces coordinate better and create more practical threats. Qxc6+ would also have been playable, leading to equality along [pv:Qxc6+ Nxc6 Kd2 O-O-O Ne2], but Qd3 preserves the edge and builds pressure that later tempts Black into 19...Qxe4, a concession that opens the door to a winning advantage.",
      "system_symbol": "!",
      "is_key_moment": true,
      "final_comment": true,
