    {
      "ply": 35,
      "san": "f5",
      "human_san": "f5",
      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "With this move\nLilienthal tell us that he has already foreseen the temporary Queen sacrifice.\nImagination and ... long sight!",
      "human_symbol": "!",
      "system_comment": "",
      "system_symbol": null,
      "is_key_moment": false,
      "final_comment": false,
      "both_present": false,
      "human_only": true,
      "system_only": false,
      "neither": false
    },
    {
      "ply": 36,
      "san": "e5",
      "human_san": "e5",
      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "18...e5 is the most accurate move, holding the balance (+0.16, Stockfish:16) along [pv:e5 Bxf6 Nxf6 dxe5 Qc5+], where White's pieces may become more passive\u2014a practical way to fight for equality when the position feels cramped....O-O was a comparable option ([pv:O-O e5 Nd5 f6 Nxe5], leads to a slight advantage for White) that could eventually win a pawn while leaving White's back rank vulnerable, but 18...e5 keeps the game level without conceding that edge.",
      "system_symbol": "!",
      "is_key_moment": true,
      "final_comment": true,
      "both_present": false,
      "human_only": false,
      "system_only": true,
      "neither": false
    },
    {
